          %h2#further_variants_of_rational_homotopy_theory Further variants of rational homotopy theory
          %p
            There are various variants of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            equipped with extra structure. This includes the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+stable+homotopy+theory"} rational stable homotopy theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} rational equivariant homotopy theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} rational equivariant stable homotopy theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+parametrized+homotopy+theory"} rational parametrized homotopy theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+parameterized+stable+homotopy+theory"} rational parameterized stable homotopy theory
          %p
            There are also several non-equivalent extensions of the notions of rational space and rationalization functor to the case of all spaces (Bousfield-Kan’s
            = succeed "-completion," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            = succeed "-rationalization" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
